## Harden Ontology Studio multi-select interactions

Context: Final browser and code review found that the click emitted after a
marquee could clear its result, context menus could retain stale selections,
map rebuilds could race dirty-panel saves, and macOS Control gestures needed
native context-menu handling. The Studio multi-select flow now preserves live
selection state across those interactions and has Playwright coverage.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-map.js
   Preserve marquee results, close stale menus, avoid panel-close races,
   share Business View persistence, handle cancellation paths, and report
   the actual multi-delete count.
2. tests/units/front/test_ontology_map_multi_select.py
   Extend contracts for click suppression, live action selection, safe map
   rebuilds, modal Escape, and shared Business View construction.
3. tests/e2e/ontology/test_studio_multi_select_flows.py
   Exercise Ctrl/Cmd marquee, empty marquee, menu freshness, canvas clearing,
   and Escape behavior in a real Chromium session.
4. docs/architecture.md
   Document Studio multi-select state, gestures, group actions, and macOS
   Control-click handling.

